			<div class="content" id="post-content-3839892">
									

<p>Can't get behind this skip. Story behind it really could use more effort put into it to try and get the reader to actually care about the characters' situation, but as it stands right now it just gives off the vibe of forcing in its themes for a cheap way to get sympathy without needing to actually develop anyone. Skips like this need more than what's presented here if you want to tell an emotional story.</p>
<p>The chat logs are unrealistically dramatic, and create a big problem with whatever immersion the article could muster, it doesn't feel like real people are messaging each other.</p>
<p>Not to mention that the safe classification makes no sense for a skip that could appear whenever a pretty common post layout is posted online, which would at the very least make it euclid on the basis of uncertainty for whether or not it could spike in activity again.</p>
<p>-1. It's not totally unsalvageable, but it'll be difficult to make it good without rewriting the whole thing.</p>

